* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary

# Fonts and web images. These were relying on `text=auto` above, which asks
# git to GUESS per file from its contents. The guess is right today, but a
# binary that happens to look text-like gets its bytes rewritten on checkout,
# and for a font that means a corrupt file with no error - and a corrupt file
# no longer byte-matches the upstream package the OFL notice in
# frontend/public/fonts/OFL.txt relies on. Declared explicitly instead.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
